  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "report_markdown": "## Executive Summary\n\n- The Unswirl peaked at 768 ft per minute in the Fan Showdown S4 Finale test.\n- The Cheater Beater (referred to as 'neater cheater beater') came in around 54.5 DBA in the Fan Showdown S4E10 test.\n- The Cheater moved forward onto season five after the S4 Finale.\n- The Cheater Beater produced 665 ft per minute of air flow in Fan Showdown S4E10.\n- The Cheater outperformed the Cheater Beater in terms of CFM/airflow.\n- The Cheater Beater did not beat the Cheater in the Fan Showdown season 4 testing.\n- The Cheater Beater placed fifth overall on the board in season 4.\n- The Cheater has been in first place since the previous season and appeared unbeatable.\n- The Cheater still remains in first place after the S4E9 test.\n\n## Findings\n\n### The Cheater's Peak Performance in the S4 Finale\nThe Cheater peaked at 776 ft per minute in the Fan Showdown S4 Finale test. This figure is corroborated by two separate accepted claims (critical=True) referencing the same test.\n\n### The Unswirl's Peak Performance in the S4 Finale\nThe Unswirl peaked at 768 ft per minute in the Fan Showdown S4 Finale test. This is lower than the Cheater's peak in the same test.\n\n### S4E9 Airflow Comparison\nIn the Fan Showdown S4E9 test, the Cheater produced 768 feet per minute of airflow, while the Cheater Beater (referred to as \"unswirl\") produced 758 feet per minute of airflow. The Cheater remained in first place after this test.\n\n### S4E10 Cheater Beater Performance\nIn the Fan Showdown S4E10 test, the Cheater Beater produced 665 feet per minute of airflow and came in around 54.5 DBA (decibels). The claim notes the fan was referred to as \"neater cheater beater\" in the evidence.\n\n### Overall Outcome and Season Progression\nThe Cheater outperformed the Cheater Beater in terms of CFM/airflow, and the Cheater Beater did not beat the Cheater in Fan Showdown season 4 testing. The Cheater Beater placed fifth overall on the board in season 4. The Cheater had been in first place since the previous season and appeared unbeatable; it moved forward onto season five after the S4 Finale.\n\n## Evidence Status\n\nAll claims were accepted by the critic. The evidence spans directly support each claim's core fact, with no hedged or qualified language requiring additional qualification. The report preserves all quantitative values (776, 768, 758, 665 ft/min; 54.5 DBA) and qualitative outcomes (first place, fifth overall, season progression) exactly as stated in the claims. No new facts were introduced.",
